WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.133
-Nice to see you again.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.300
We have so much to talk about.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.467
I'm so happy to be here
with you.

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:05.634
-Please, thank you
for coming back.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.467
Last time we talked
was right before you won

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:10.801
a Grammy and an Oscar
for "Fight For You."

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:12.067
-Yes.
-Congratulations.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:13.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you, thank you.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.968
-From "Judas and
the Black Messiah."

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:18.501
I mean, wow,
you have an Oscar.

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:20.234
-Yeah, it's crazy.

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:21.501
-What was the night
like for you?

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:23.200
Did you just --
-Oh, my gosh, it was amazing.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.367
And they only let you
bring one guest.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:29.067
So, it was not craziness
like most awards show times

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:30.667
because of COVID.

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:33.367
And it was just me and my mom,
and she was so excited.

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:35.367
We got to meet everybody.
It was chill.

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:37.267
Angela Bassett came up to us.

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:38.934
She was like, "Oh, my gosh!
Is this your mom?"

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:40.701
[ Cheers ]
"This is crazy."

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:44.667
And Zendaya presented you
with your Oscar,

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:47.133
and she did
a little jump for joy.

00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:48.801
-Oh, my gosh.
-You guys must know each other,

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:50.334
I'm assuming.
-Yeah, actually, we both grew up

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:52.968
in the Bay Area.
And I met her when we were kids

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:54.801
'cause we were supposed to be
in a band together,

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:56.467
which is super random.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.067
But we ended up
not being in a band together,

00:00:58.067 --> 00:01:00.968
and then, years later,
we see each other, and, yeah.

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:02.000
It's like a reunion.
-At the Oscars.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.033
Oh, my God, yeah.

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:04.400
And now where do you have
the Oscar?

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.834
Is it next to your Grammys?
Where do you put it?

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:07.801
-It's funny, I keep it
on my dining table

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.434
so when people come into
my house, they're like,

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:11.234
"Is that...real?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.334
"Is that...?"
I'm like, "Yeah, pick it up.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:14.968
It's heavy."
-That's exactly right.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:16.200
Is it really heavy?
-Yes, it is.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.033
It's super heavy.
-I'll never know.

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:19.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.968
Speaking of Grammys,
you're nominated this year

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:24.968
for your work on Mary J. Blige's
album, "Good Morning Gorgeous."

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.434
-Yeah, that was awesome.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:28.734
Thank you.

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:30.501
-I love Mary J. Blige.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:33.033
But this is -- you worked on --
actually, that song,

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:36.701
and produced the -- co-wrote
and produced that song with her.

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:39.000
And she's one of your idols,
you said?

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.133
-Yeah, one of
my favorite artists.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.734
I grew up listening
to Mary J. Blige.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.100
I used to sing her songs
on piano.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.133
And it's just, like, crazy that
I even got the opportunity

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.267
to work with her, so...
-How did you get into Mary J.

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:51.567
when you're going up?
-It was my mom.

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:53.000
You know, she was
going through some stuff,

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.267
so she would listen to it.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:58.133
And I didn't understand it
at the time, but I get it now.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:00.133
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:04.000
Well, you also were listening
to Lenny Kravitz, Alicia Keys,

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.734
Stevie Wonder.
And I just saw that

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:09.534
you actually performed
with all of those people.

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:11.133
-Yeah, it's crazy.
-What is it like --

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:14.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.300
What is it like
to share the stage

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.267
with all these artists
that you were inspired by?

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:19.367
-I mean, it's insane.
Like, these are people

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:21.434
I grew up watching
and listening,

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:24.267
and the fact that
they show me so much love,

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:25.667
and I got to perform with them,

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:29.200
it's nerve wracking but also
just, like, confirmation.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.467
Like, I'm exactly
where I'm supposed to be.

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.968
-Yeah.
You are.

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:34.234
You're where
you're supposed to be, yeah.

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:36.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.767
-Can we talk about
"Beauty and the Beast"?

00:02:37.767 --> 00:02:39.033
-Yes.
-You can add this now

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.434
to your résumé.
-I know, I'm a Disney Princess!

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:42.667
-You're a Disney Princess.
Exactly right! Yes!

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:44.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.868
♪♪

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:50.868
Here's a picture of you as Belle
right there.

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:55.567
This is -- This is one of
my favorite Disney cartoons.

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:59.467
I love it. I mean, this is
pre-Pixar and Lin-Manuel.

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:01.634
"Beauty and the Beast" was --
that's my jam.

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:03.834
Was this a dream for you
to be a princess?

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:06.300
-Absolutely.
It was definitely, like,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.067
something I imagined to be
as a kid,

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:11.167
but you never really think
it could happen.

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:13.367
So, I'm walking
a little different.

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:14.634
I'm talking a little different.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:15.934
-You are.
-You know?

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:17.901
-You also go
by your real name in this.

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.868
It's Gabriella Wilson.
-Yeah.

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:21.334
-When you're doing a new thing
or you're acting,

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.000
you want to go by that name?
-Yeah, you know,

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.567
for a long time,
I was in the shadows.

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:27.801
And I really wanted people
to focus on the music.

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:29.701
And now that I'm doing
other things,

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:32.200
I feel like it's time for people
to get to know the person

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.167
behind the music.
-Yeah.

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:37.300
I love that.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:41.033
What can everyone expect
when they watch this,

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:42.400
"Beauty and the Beast"?

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.033
-It's exactly what it's called,
a celebration.

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:47.434
You know, this is the
anniversary -- 30 years.

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:49.901
So, it's gonna be live-action.

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:52.434
Of course, with me
and the most amazing cast.

00:03:52.434 --> 00:03:54.267
Martin Short, who's here.
-Yeah, come on.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.734
Oh, my gosh.
[ Applause ]

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:58.767
-David Alan Grier, Rita Moreno,
Josh Groban.

00:03:58.767 --> 00:03:59.901
-Josh Groban I saw
is in it, too.

00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:01.334
-Yeah.
Shania Twain.

00:04:01.334 --> 00:04:03.000
-Yes! Oh, I know that!
[ Cheers ]

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.300
-It's crazy.
But it's gonna be

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.868
the cartoon and then
into the live-action.

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:10.000
And it's just gonna be
a beautiful celebration.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.334
We're gonna celebrate
the creation of it.

00:04:12.334 --> 00:04:14.067
-Yeah.
I have another close-up picture

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:16.033
of you looking gorgeous
as Belle.

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:17.267
-Thank you.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:19.467
-I wanted to
show a clip tonight,

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:21.534
but we don't actually
have a clip.

00:04:21.534 --> 00:04:23.734
But we do have a ukulele.

00:04:23.734 --> 00:04:25.067
-Oh!
Okay.

00:04:25.067 --> 00:04:27.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
-And I was just wondering...

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.734
if you wouldn't mind giving --

00:04:29.734 --> 00:04:31.167
Could you maybe give us
a little taste?

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:32.167
-Okay.
[ Clears throat ]

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:35.467
Let's see.
Let's see what I can do.

00:04:35.467 --> 00:04:36.934
♪♪

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:40.033
♪ Certain as the sun ♪

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:42.367
♪♪

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:44.767
♪ Rising in the East ♪

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:46.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:49.934
♪ Tale as old as time ♪

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:53.501
♪ Song as old as rhyme ♪

00:04:53.501 --> 00:05:01.167
♪ Beauty and the Beast ♪

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:06.934
♪♪

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:08.100
-H.E.R., everybody!

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:10.634
"Beauty and the Beast:
A 30th Celebration"

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:14.033
airs December 15th
at 8:00 p.m., on ABC.

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:16.100
Mary McCartney
joins us after the break.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:17.634
Stick around.
I tried!

